1
00:00:00,567 --> 00:00:01,167
<i> You're leaving, Peter?</i>

2
00:00:01,300 --> 00:00:01,900
<i> You're going back to Manila?</i>

3
00:00:02,033 --> 00:00:03,133
<i> Jin Ho, what happened to you?</i>

4
00:00:03,267 --> 00:00:04,967
<i>It's nothing,
it's just work hazard.</i>

5
00:00:05,100 --> 00:00:07,300
<i>Enjoy your coffee
because that'll be your last.</i>

6
00:00:07,433 --> 00:00:08,933
<i> You're Kang Dae-Hyun.</i>

7
00:00:09,067 --> 00:00:10,133
<i> [THUDS]</i>

8
00:00:10,267 --> 00:00:12,267
<i>The cops already know
who I really am.</i>

9
00:00:12,400 --> 00:00:13,333
<i> I knew it!</i>

10
00:00:13,467 --> 00:00:15,200
<i>Berdugo, I think I saw Delgado.</i>

11
00:00:15,333 --> 00:00:17,333
<i>Has your husband's body
been released?</i>

12
00:00:17,467 --> 00:00:18,567
<i> Not yet.</i>

13
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:20,233
<i> It's not impossible
for the syndicate to have doubts</i>

14
00:00:20,367 --> 00:00:22,000
<i>as long as they don't see
your body.</i>

15
00:00:22,133 --> 00:00:24,100
<i> Then, let's bury Miguel.</i>

16
00:00:24,233 --> 00:00:25,600
<i> I'm going to the wake.</i>

17
00:00:25,733 --> 00:00:26,533
<i> Who died?</i>

18
00:00:26,667 --> 00:00:27,733
<i> Didn't Joey tell you?</i>

19
00:00:27,867 --> 00:00:29,100
<i>You're going to Delgado's wake?</i>

20
00:00:29,233 --> 00:00:31,133
<i>- Yes, Hon.
- I'll come with you.</i>

21
00:00:33,267 --> 00:00:35,533
<i> [OBB]</i>

22
00:00:49,767 --> 00:00:51,567
Boss, are you okay?

23
00:00:53,967 --> 00:00:54,967
Oh, yes.

24
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:56,100
It's just my sister.

25
00:00:56,233 --> 00:00:59,400
She told me something
but I feel like it's fake.

26
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:01,333
But everything's fine.

27
00:01:01,467 --> 00:01:02,533
Are you sure?

28
00:01:02,667 --> 00:01:04,333
Do you want us to stay with you?

29
00:01:06,933 --> 00:01:07,967
[LIGHT MUSIC PLAYING]

30
00:01:08,133 --> 00:01:09,500
Let's not enter the picture.

31
00:01:09,633 --> 00:01:11,933
Boss Idol already has company.

32
00:01:12,067 --> 00:01:13,267
Hi, Andrew.

33
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:14,567
Hi, Zoey.

34
00:01:14,700 --> 00:01:16,367
How's mommy?

35
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:19,433
Well, it's still a waiting game.

36
00:01:19,567 --> 00:01:22,333
[CHUCKLES SOFTLY]
You know, don't worry.

37
00:01:22,467 --> 00:01:23,900
I already filed a leave
of absence from work

38
00:01:24,033 --> 00:01:26,000
so I can stay with you.

39
00:01:27,433 --> 00:01:29,067
Oh, that's perfect,

40
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:33,000
because Kyle, Elai,
and I have somewhere to go.

41
00:01:33,133 --> 00:01:34,933
- We do?
- Yes.

42
00:01:35,067 --> 00:01:36,133
That thing you had signed.

43
00:01:36,267 --> 00:01:38,500
- Ah!
- Yes, I almost forgot.

44
00:01:38,633 --> 00:01:40,400
Yes, there is,
that's right.

45
00:01:40,567 --> 00:01:42,667
Oh, wait,
you're leaving me here?

46
00:01:42,800 --> 00:01:45,200
Yes, don't you want
to watch over mommy?

47
00:01:45,333 --> 00:01:47,733
I really have somewhere to go.

48
00:01:47,867 --> 00:01:48,833
[♪CURIOUS MUSIC PLAYING♪]

49
00:01:48,967 --> 00:01:50,933
So, if it's okay,

50
00:01:51,067 --> 00:01:52,867
can you stay with mommy?

51
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,700
Of course, yes!

52
00:01:56,633 --> 00:01:57,667
Perfect.

53
00:01:59,267 --> 00:02:00,933
Just tell me...

54
00:02:01,067 --> 00:02:02,733
if you need anything,

55
00:02:02,867 --> 00:02:04,900
and if something happens
to mommy.

56
00:02:05,033 --> 00:02:07,200
I'll come back right away.

57
00:02:07,333 --> 00:02:08,333
Yeah.

58
00:02:08,467 --> 00:02:11,067
So, shall we?

59
00:02:11,200 --> 00:02:12,467
Let's go.

60
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:14,467
Okay, okay, take care.

61
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:18,100
Bye.

62
00:02:18,233 --> 00:02:22,267
[CURIOUS MUSIC CONTINUES]

63
00:02:23,567 --> 00:02:24,800
<i> Just help yourselves, okay?</i>

64
00:02:24,933 --> 00:02:25,733
[PHONE CHIMES]

65
00:02:25,867 --> 00:02:27,167
Go ahead, help yourselves.

66
00:02:37,067 --> 00:02:38,600
Here, get this too, okay?

67
00:02:39,600 --> 00:02:41,333
Go ahead, help yourselves.

68
00:02:43,867 --> 00:02:44,800
Wait a moment.

69
00:02:44,933 --> 00:02:46,267
Please excuse me.

70
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:47,933
Ma'am, Sir.

71
00:02:48,100 --> 00:02:49,800
[♪UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING♪]

72
00:02:49,933 --> 00:02:51,367
- My condolences.
- My condolences.

73
00:02:51,500 --> 00:02:52,633
Thank you.

74
00:02:52,867 --> 00:02:55,967
I know I've said this before,

75
00:02:56,100 --> 00:02:58,033
but I'm offering my condolences.

76
00:02:59,267 --> 00:03:00,967
Thank you, Ma'am.

77
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:03,200
We just brought
a little something.

78
00:03:03,333 --> 00:03:05,800
Oh, you shouldn't have,

79
00:03:05,933 --> 00:03:08,933
but thank you very much.

80
00:03:09,067 --> 00:03:12,200
We take care of other people.

81
00:03:12,333 --> 00:03:15,733
Of course, we have to take care
of our own.

82
00:03:17,133 --> 00:03:18,500
Thank you.

83
00:03:19,967 --> 00:03:21,433
Why is it closed?

84
00:03:22,833 --> 00:03:25,900
Because of what happened
to my husband,

85
00:03:26,033 --> 00:03:30,567
we still can't bear
to see...

86
00:03:30,700 --> 00:03:32,833
what happened to him.

87
00:03:32,967 --> 00:03:36,733
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

88
00:03:37,467 --> 00:03:38,933
I'll just prepare this.

89
00:03:39,067 --> 00:03:40,067
Please sit down.

90
00:03:40,200 --> 00:03:41,800
I'll help you.

91
00:03:41,933 --> 00:03:43,733
- Okay.
- Let's start here.

92
00:03:46,467 --> 00:03:48,600
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

93
00:03:48,733 --> 00:03:52,733
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

94
00:03:56,433 --> 00:03:58,767
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

95
00:03:58,900 --> 00:04:01,233
What brings you here?

96
00:04:01,367 --> 00:04:03,067
What is this? A spot check?

97
00:04:04,033 --> 00:04:05,800
Is Berdugo with you?

98
00:04:05,933 --> 00:04:07,267
No.

99
00:04:07,400 --> 00:04:08,767
Why are you looking for him?

100
00:04:08,900 --> 00:04:11,267
Because I wasn't expecting you.

101
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:12,933
What do you need?

102
00:04:13,067 --> 00:04:15,267
Where's your boyfriend?

103
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:18,100
That man needs
to explain himself.

104
00:04:18,233 --> 00:04:20,533
I saw him being chased
by the cops.

105
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:25,000
If you're here
to report and blame him,

106
00:04:25,133 --> 00:04:26,533
there's no need.

107
00:04:26,667 --> 00:04:29,933
He told me everything,
so I told him to lay low.

108
00:04:30,833 --> 00:04:32,667
So, you can leave now.

109
00:04:33,667 --> 00:04:35,767
Let me show you these photos.

110
00:04:36,133 --> 00:04:37,767
Probably, you have no idea.

111
00:04:37,900 --> 00:04:41,700
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

112
00:04:44,633 --> 00:04:47,067
Did he tell you
he was with a woman?

113
00:04:57,333 --> 00:04:59,467
Ma'am, let me take care of this.

114
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:00,700
I can handle it.

115
00:05:00,867 --> 00:05:02,733
Just sit down.

116
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,800
You take care of mommy,

117
00:05:04,933 --> 00:05:06,433
and I value that.

118
00:05:06,567 --> 00:05:07,600
So let me do this.

119
00:05:07,733 --> 00:05:09,433
It's just a small thing.

120
00:05:10,900 --> 00:05:12,867
Thank you so much, Ma'am.

121
00:05:13,200 --> 00:05:14,700
You're really kind.

122
00:05:15,833 --> 00:05:18,367
Sir Tomas is lucky to have you.

123
00:05:19,833 --> 00:05:22,033
I'm lucky to have him too.

124
00:05:22,167 --> 00:05:26,133
You know, even before we met,

125
00:05:26,267 --> 00:05:28,933
he was already working with mom.

126
00:05:29,067 --> 00:05:32,433
And you know how picky
mom is with people?

127
00:05:32,567 --> 00:05:34,067
Oh, yes.
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

128
00:05:34,200 --> 00:05:38,033
I was nervous
when I first met her.

129
00:05:38,700 --> 00:05:40,167
That's how mommy is.

130
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:43,100
But since she and Tomas
get along,

131
00:05:43,233 --> 00:05:45,933
you know,
I know I can trust him.

132
00:05:46,067 --> 00:05:49,000
Even if he's quiet and,
you know,

133
00:05:49,133 --> 00:05:50,733
a bit aloof.

134
00:05:50,867 --> 00:05:54,900
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

135
00:06:03,233 --> 00:06:07,367
[FOREBODING MUSIC PLAYING]

136
00:06:20,200 --> 00:06:24,633
[FOREBODING MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

137
00:06:27,400 --> 00:06:29,200
Bring out Jin Ho.

138
00:06:30,233 --> 00:06:31,967
I need to confront him.
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

139
00:06:32,933 --> 00:06:34,700
If you want me to,
I'll finish him off too.

140
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:38,700
What, Liza?

141
00:06:38,833 --> 00:06:40,100
Leave me alone!

142
00:06:40,433 --> 00:06:42,200
I'm furious at that man!

143
00:06:44,167 --> 00:06:45,100
Don't.

144
00:06:45,233 --> 00:06:46,800
It's too soon.

145
00:06:47,900 --> 00:06:51,000
We can still use
what we learned from him.

146
00:06:52,400 --> 00:06:53,967
What's your plan?

147
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:57,600
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

148
00:07:01,133 --> 00:07:02,800
Sir!

149
00:07:02,933 --> 00:07:04,533
Don't open that, Sir.

150
00:07:06,067 --> 00:07:07,433
Sorry.

151
00:07:08,867 --> 00:07:10,700
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

152
00:07:10,833 --> 00:07:12,933
Hon, what happened?

153
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:17,467
I just wanted to look.

154
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:18,933
Why, Sir?

155
00:07:19,067 --> 00:07:20,633
Sorry, Clarissa.

156
00:07:20,767 --> 00:07:23,400
I was just curious about
what happened to your husband.

157
00:07:23,533 --> 00:07:26,367
Hon, that's rude.

158
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:28,833
They don't want to show it,
right?

159
00:07:30,467 --> 00:07:32,400
I feel so embarrassed.

160
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:35,100
I'm so sorry, Clarissa.

161
00:07:36,167 --> 00:07:37,400
Sorry, too.

162
00:07:37,733 --> 00:07:39,967
Curiosity got the best of me.

163
00:07:40,100 --> 00:07:41,233
It's okay, Sir.

164
00:07:41,367 --> 00:07:43,000
Don't worry about it.

165
00:07:43,133 --> 00:07:45,967
No, it's not okay.

166
00:07:46,100 --> 00:07:47,367
It's not okay.

167
00:07:48,733 --> 00:07:49,700
I apologize.

168
00:07:49,833 --> 00:07:53,267
We better go.

169
00:07:54,167 --> 00:07:55,533
Let's go home.

170
00:07:55,667 --> 00:07:58,433
Sorry again, Clarissa.

171
00:07:58,567 --> 00:08:00,467
My wife is right.

172
00:08:00,600 --> 00:08:03,467
I don't want to make it awkward
at your husband's wake,

173
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:05,167
so we'll go ahead.

174
00:08:07,167 --> 00:08:10,133
If we can help you in any way,

175
00:08:10,267 --> 00:08:12,167
just tell us, okay?

176
00:08:12,400 --> 00:08:13,267
We'll go ahead.

177
00:08:13,400 --> 00:08:16,367
Thank you, thank you both.

178
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:20,400
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

179
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:28,200
- I wonder who else came.
- That's right.

180
00:08:28,333 --> 00:08:29,700
I feel like a lot of people
went there.

181
00:08:29,833 --> 00:08:31,100
It's Joey.

182
00:08:31,233 --> 00:08:33,100
Joey.

183
00:08:33,233 --> 00:08:35,300
Elai, Kyle.

184
00:08:37,200 --> 00:08:39,067
Our condolences.

185
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:41,333
Joey, my condolences
for your father's passing.

186
00:08:42,367 --> 00:08:43,633
Thank you.

187
00:08:44,767 --> 00:08:46,667
How did you know?
[MELLOW MUSIC PLAYING]

188
00:08:46,800 --> 00:08:48,700
How else?

189
00:08:48,833 --> 00:08:51,267
From our great reporter.

190
00:08:54,367 --> 00:08:58,533
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

191
00:09:13,600 --> 00:09:18,100
[ROMANTIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

192
00:09:31,833 --> 00:09:35,633
[HEART POUNDING]

193
00:09:35,767 --> 00:09:41,633
[ROMANTIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

194
00:09:51,167 --> 00:09:53,167
Come on, let's bring
this inside first.

195
00:09:53,300 --> 00:09:54,267
- Yes, all right.
- I'll do it.

196
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:56,667
Boss, I'll take care of that.

197
00:09:56,800 --> 00:09:58,533
[INDISTINCT CHATTER]

198
00:09:58,667 --> 00:10:00,233
Thank you.

199
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:08,933
Condolences?

200
00:10:09,067 --> 00:10:10,567
You're not sure?
[LIGHT PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

201
00:10:10,800 --> 00:10:14,033
Because I'm sure there's really
no one to mourn for.

202
00:10:14,300 --> 00:10:15,300
Hey!

203
00:10:17,567 --> 00:10:19,867
You know we need to do this.

204
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,700
This way,
no one will ask about dad.

205
00:10:23,933 --> 00:10:25,900
But thank you for coming

206
00:10:26,033 --> 00:10:28,600
even though you know
this isn't real.

207
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:33,867
I want to know
what happened to you.

208
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:36,500
And actually,

209
00:10:36,667 --> 00:10:39,467
I should have visited you
before.

210
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:42,833
[ROMANTIC MUSIC PLAYING]

211
00:10:42,967 --> 00:10:44,600
Me too.

212
00:10:45,767 --> 00:10:48,533
I think I should have exerted
more effort.

213
00:10:49,567 --> 00:10:51,233
I mean, I should have
checked on you

214
00:10:51,367 --> 00:10:54,033
because you're also going
through things with your family.

215
00:10:57,767 --> 00:11:00,833
Honestly, I really
wanted to talk to you.

216
00:11:00,967 --> 00:11:04,233
But of course, I didn't want
any trouble.

217
00:11:06,867 --> 00:11:08,733
Trouble?

218
00:11:08,900 --> 00:11:11,767
Why would you say that, Joey?

219
00:11:11,900 --> 00:11:17,167
Well, of course, if Zoey
finds out I'm talking to you,

220
00:11:17,300 --> 00:11:19,300
she might get mad at me.

221
00:11:22,300 --> 00:11:25,500
Wait, there's nothing wrong
if we talk, right?

222
00:11:26,367 --> 00:11:27,233
We're...

223
00:11:27,367 --> 00:11:29,167
We're friends.

224
00:11:30,167 --> 00:11:31,567
Of course.

225
00:11:31,700 --> 00:11:33,033
I just mean,

226
00:11:33,167 --> 00:11:35,267
if she sees me talking to you,

227
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:37,233
and she wants you two
to be okay,

228
00:11:37,367 --> 00:11:38,467
or to get back together,

229
00:11:38,600 --> 00:11:41,600
she might say I'm meddling
in between, right?

230
00:11:41,767 --> 00:11:45,933
[ROMANTIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

231
00:11:56,600 --> 00:12:00,733
[ROMANTIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

232
00:12:07,867 --> 00:12:11,067
[ENGINE REVVING]

233
00:12:11,200 --> 00:12:15,800
[ROMANTIC MUSIC CONTINUES]

234
00:12:17,100 --> 00:12:20,133
Well, we're not together.

235
00:12:21,067 --> 00:12:23,100
There's nothing between us.

236
00:12:24,833 --> 00:12:26,433
But if...

237
00:12:26,867 --> 00:12:28,667
we do become a couple,

238
00:12:30,867 --> 00:12:34,500
of course,
I'd want to maintain...

239
00:12:34,633 --> 00:12:37,967
the friendship we have, right?

240
00:12:39,233 --> 00:12:40,967
Really?

241
00:12:42,233 --> 00:12:44,233
Yes.

242
00:12:44,367 --> 00:12:48,500
But I hope you don't believe
the rumors anymore.

243
00:12:49,400 --> 00:12:53,500
Believe reliable sources like...

244
00:12:54,233 --> 00:12:55,633
me.

245
00:13:01,667 --> 00:13:04,700
Speaking of reliable sources...

246
00:13:06,433 --> 00:13:08,367
I have a story for you.

247
00:13:08,500 --> 00:13:10,367
It's not just from
a reliable source,

248
00:13:10,500 --> 00:13:12,233
I actually confirmed it.

249
00:13:12,367 --> 00:13:14,400
Okay, what is it?

250
00:13:14,533 --> 00:13:17,233
Jin Ho, he's an enemy.
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

251
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:20,100
I'll tell you everything inside.

252
00:13:20,233 --> 00:13:21,600
Even I was shocked.

253
00:13:21,767 --> 00:13:23,767
Of course, we trusted him.

254
00:13:29,333 --> 00:13:31,167
Okay.

255
00:13:31,300 --> 00:13:35,433
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

256
00:13:36,533 --> 00:13:37,933
I knew it.

257
00:13:38,067 --> 00:13:39,967
My instincts were telling me...

258
00:13:40,267 --> 00:13:43,033
there was something off
about that man.

259
00:13:44,133 --> 00:13:46,600
That's why you had
a bad feeling about him.

260
00:13:47,167 --> 00:13:50,233
And from the start,
you were irritated with him.

261
00:13:50,367 --> 00:13:52,733
Then you always contradicted
each other.

262
00:13:56,033 --> 00:13:57,067
Jin Ho?

263
00:13:57,200 --> 00:14:01,633
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

264
00:14:05,300 --> 00:14:06,967
- Joey?
- Peter?

265
00:14:08,633 --> 00:14:10,833
Joey! Joey!

266
00:14:10,967 --> 00:14:13,433
[EMOTIONAL MUSIC PLAYING]

267
00:14:13,700 --> 00:14:15,200
Sorry, I came right away

268
00:14:15,333 --> 00:14:17,033
when I heard about
your father's wake.

269
00:14:17,167 --> 00:14:18,467
Sorry I didn't...

270
00:14:18,600 --> 00:14:19,400
I didn't comfort you right away.

271
00:14:19,533 --> 00:14:20,800
Sorry.

272
00:14:22,867 --> 00:14:24,467
Are you crying?

273
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:26,700
Of course, I'm sad for you.

274
00:14:28,267 --> 00:14:30,000
You're smiling?

275
00:14:30,133 --> 00:14:32,600
Are you angry at your father,
that's why you're smiling?

276
00:14:35,167 --> 00:14:36,667
Should I tell him?

277
00:14:40,633 --> 00:14:42,800
He is our friend.

278
00:14:42,933 --> 00:14:44,400
I trust him.

279
00:14:47,133 --> 00:14:49,000
Don't react, okay.

280
00:14:51,367 --> 00:14:54,167
Miguel Delgado is still alive.

281
00:14:54,300 --> 00:14:55,300
What?

282
00:14:55,433 --> 00:14:57,967
- Watch your mouth.
- I said don't react.

283
00:14:58,100 --> 00:15:00,067
[CURIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

284
00:15:00,200 --> 00:15:02,933
So, you almost caught Berdugo,

285
00:15:03,100 --> 00:15:04,833
the leader of the syndicate,

286
00:15:04,967 --> 00:15:07,200
but he escaped?
[LIGHT PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

287
00:15:07,533 --> 00:15:08,833
Yes.

288
00:15:08,967 --> 00:15:11,667
Then your father almost died

289
00:15:11,800 --> 00:15:13,633
because Berdugo was hunting him.

290
00:15:14,667 --> 00:15:16,267
That's why you pretended
he was dead.

291
00:15:16,400 --> 00:15:17,900
Hush.

292
00:15:18,033 --> 00:15:19,467
That's why there's a wake.

293
00:15:22,967 --> 00:15:24,200
Then Jin Ho turned out to be

294
00:15:24,333 --> 00:15:26,900
a member of
the Korean syndicate.

295
00:15:27,033 --> 00:15:28,800
He wasn't really part
of the interpol.

296
00:15:29,633 --> 00:15:33,467
And what? He only used us
to find his girlfriend?

297
00:15:36,467 --> 00:15:37,367
Wow!

298
00:15:37,500 --> 00:15:39,400
Information overload!

299
00:15:41,867 --> 00:15:43,567
Hard to believe.

300
00:15:43,700 --> 00:15:45,900
I thought that oppa
was my best friend.

301
00:15:46,033 --> 00:15:47,667
[PLEASANT MUSIC PLAYING]

302
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:49,233
So that's why...

303
00:15:50,033 --> 00:15:52,633
you've got that oppa vibe now,
right?

304
00:15:52,767 --> 00:15:54,533
I even thought you were Jin Ho.

305
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:57,367
Hello.

306
00:15:57,500 --> 00:15:59,000
[CHUCKLES]

307
00:15:59,967 --> 00:16:01,567
[SIGHS]
It's so hard being away

308
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:02,633
for a long time.

309
00:16:02,767 --> 00:16:05,067
You don't get updated
about what's happening.

310
00:16:06,467 --> 00:16:07,433
Sorry, okay?

311
00:16:07,567 --> 00:16:09,667
I wasn't able to help you.

312
00:16:10,933 --> 00:16:12,567
But that's fine.

313
00:16:12,700 --> 00:16:15,067
Do you know why?
Because I'm here now.

314
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:17,233
- Yes.
- Even if it's just us three,

315
00:16:17,367 --> 00:16:20,000
we're complete!
We're still a group.

316
00:16:20,133 --> 00:16:21,800
- Yes.
- Right?

317
00:16:21,933 --> 00:16:23,200
Complete!

318
00:16:25,133 --> 00:16:26,833
Peter, Andrew, Joey.

319
00:16:26,967 --> 00:16:28,067
What?

320
00:16:28,200 --> 00:16:32,200
[PLEASANT MUSIC CONTINUES]

321
00:16:33,133 --> 00:16:34,400
Come on.

322
00:16:34,533 --> 00:16:36,400
- Yes!
- Never say die.

323
00:16:36,533 --> 00:16:38,433
Never say die.

324
00:16:41,467 --> 00:16:42,867
Oh, Andrew.

325
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,300
Yvette.

326
00:16:44,433 --> 00:16:46,367
Why are you here?

327
00:16:46,500 --> 00:16:49,000
Who's watching mommy
at the hospital?

328
00:16:49,133 --> 00:16:50,700
Zoey.

329
00:16:50,833 --> 00:16:52,767
I just had to...

330
00:16:52,900 --> 00:16:55,733
drop by the wake of Joey's dad,

331
00:16:55,867 --> 00:16:57,367
before I go back
to the hospital.

332
00:16:57,500 --> 00:16:58,567
Okay.

333
00:16:58,700 --> 00:17:00,900
Well, we also went home
right away.

334
00:17:01,033 --> 00:17:03,667
Because Tomas and I
had a discussion.

335
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:05,400
Discussion?

336
00:17:05,533 --> 00:17:06,900
You mean you argued?

337
00:17:07,033 --> 00:17:09,267
Just a little misunderstanding.

338
00:17:09,400 --> 00:17:10,833
We'll be okay.

339
00:17:10,967 --> 00:17:12,733
That's how we are
when we have disagreements.

340
00:17:12,867 --> 00:17:16,467
You know, we just need space
from each other.

341
00:17:16,633 --> 00:17:17,633
But we'll be okay.

342
00:17:17,767 --> 00:17:20,100
Soon, he'll be back.

343
00:17:20,233 --> 00:17:21,833
Uncle Andrew!

344
00:17:21,967 --> 00:17:23,767
Uncle Andrew!

345
00:17:23,900 --> 00:17:24,800
I knew it,

346
00:17:24,933 --> 00:17:26,933
you were the one who arrived.

347
00:17:27,067 --> 00:17:28,633
It's late.
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

348
00:17:28,767 --> 00:17:30,267
Where's Kisses?

349
00:17:30,400 --> 00:17:31,900
She's in her room.

350
00:17:32,033 --> 00:17:35,700
Uncle, can you help me here?

351
00:17:35,833 --> 00:17:38,967
[OMINOUS MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

352
00:17:43,867 --> 00:17:45,167
Okay.

353
00:17:45,300 --> 00:17:47,533
It's all chill back home.

354
00:17:47,667 --> 00:17:50,267
You know? Life is simple
in the province, quiet.

355
00:17:50,433 --> 00:17:52,567
I even missed the noise.

356
00:17:53,933 --> 00:17:56,900
Why don't you just stay here
again?

357
00:17:59,200 --> 00:18:01,800
That's my plan, but I came
earlier than expected

358
00:18:01,933 --> 00:18:05,533
because I thought Uncle Miguel
was gone so...

359
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:10,000
Sorry, you got worried.

360
00:18:10,133 --> 00:18:12,600
What are you saying?
That's fine.

361
00:18:12,733 --> 00:18:15,867
Well, I also intended
to learn from Jin Ho.

362
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:19,433
But it turns out he wasn't
a part of the interpol.

363
00:18:20,367 --> 00:18:23,233
You know? I really wanted
to be a secret agent.

364
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:25,967
That's what I wanted.
It's so cool.

365
00:18:26,100 --> 00:18:29,100
He really looked like
a secret agent.

366
00:18:29,233 --> 00:18:31,167
But in the end,

367
00:18:31,300 --> 00:18:33,567
he kept secrets from us.

368
00:18:33,700 --> 00:18:35,767
Never mind, that's fine.

369
00:18:35,900 --> 00:18:38,300
I'll still find a way
to achieve that.

370
00:18:40,367 --> 00:18:42,033
Uncle Miguel! That's it!

371
00:18:42,167 --> 00:18:44,233
- He's my idol now.
- Hush! You're so noisy.

372
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:48,000
Wait...

373
00:18:48,133 --> 00:18:50,233
if the coffin is empty,

374
00:18:50,367 --> 00:18:52,000
then where's your father?

375
00:18:54,367 --> 00:18:55,700
Do you want to know?

376
00:18:55,867 --> 00:18:57,400
- Where?
- Come.

377
00:18:59,267 --> 00:19:00,067
Secret.

378
00:19:00,200 --> 00:19:04,800
[PLAYFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

379
00:19:07,600 --> 00:19:08,267
Yes, Sir.

380
00:19:08,400 --> 00:19:10,400
I'm just here, I'm not leaving.

381
00:19:10,533 --> 00:19:11,400
Good.

382
00:19:11,533 --> 00:19:12,800
Yes, partner.

383
00:19:12,933 --> 00:19:15,367
Don't ever show yourself
to other people,

384
00:19:15,500 --> 00:19:19,633
especially now, they might think
you're a ghost.

385
00:19:19,767 --> 00:19:21,333
The one I want to haunt...

386
00:19:21,467 --> 00:19:23,133
is Berdugo.

387
00:19:23,267 --> 00:19:25,100
That's why we need to find him.

388
00:19:25,233 --> 00:19:26,767
<i>By the way, Cruz.
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

389
00:19:26,900 --> 00:19:29,500
That car I asked you to trace,

390
00:19:29,667 --> 00:19:31,067
what's the update?

391
00:19:31,200 --> 00:19:34,267
Nothing yet, they haven't
gotten back to me.

392
00:19:34,400 --> 00:19:36,533
<i>But if that car
belongs to Jin Ho,</i>

393
00:19:36,667 --> 00:19:38,933
most likely the name on
the registration is different.

394
00:19:39,067 --> 00:19:40,500
Maybe even fake.

395
00:19:40,633 --> 00:19:43,000
Okay, just follow it up

396
00:19:43,133 --> 00:19:46,633
<i>so we can confirm our suspicion
about Jin Ho,</i>

397
00:19:46,767 --> 00:19:48,667
that he's with Berdugo.

398
00:19:48,800 --> 00:19:51,267
We'll take care of that,
Major Delgado.

399
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:53,067
Just stay put.

400
00:19:53,200 --> 00:19:55,333
For now, let's focus...

401
00:19:55,467 --> 00:19:57,133
<i> on tomorrow's plan...</i>

402
00:19:57,267 --> 00:19:59,000
for your burial.

403
00:19:59,133 --> 00:20:00,733
Ten-four, Chief.

404
00:20:05,900 --> 00:20:09,867
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

405
00:20:14,567 --> 00:20:16,267
This looks old.

406
00:20:17,367 --> 00:20:20,233
Did you get this
from the teddy bear?

407
00:20:20,367 --> 00:20:22,600
Yes, Kisses found it.

408
00:20:24,867 --> 00:20:26,267
Okay, wait.

409
00:20:27,600 --> 00:20:29,967
We need a cable,

410
00:20:30,100 --> 00:20:33,100
like the one for an SLR camera.

411
00:20:35,633 --> 00:20:36,633
Let's see.

412
00:20:36,767 --> 00:20:38,067
Hopefully, it works.

413
00:20:38,200 --> 00:20:42,300
[OMINOUS MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

414
00:20:46,433 --> 00:20:47,933
[BLIPS]

415
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:54,333
[CLICKING]

416
00:20:54,467 --> 00:20:55,200
[BLIPS]

417
00:20:55,333 --> 00:20:59,900
[♪STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING♪]

418
00:21:05,600 --> 00:21:10,167
[PHONE RINGING]

419
00:21:11,900 --> 00:21:13,400
Hello?

420
00:21:13,533 --> 00:21:14,833
Yes, speaking.

421
00:21:18,500 --> 00:21:19,800
Mommy is awake?

422
00:21:19,933 --> 00:21:25,333
[STIRRING MUSIC INTENSIFIES]

423
00:21:25,633 --> 00:21:27,233
Mommy! Mommy!
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

424
00:21:27,367 --> 00:21:30,167
- Uncle, can we come?
- Mommy! Mommy!

425
00:21:30,300 --> 00:21:33,067
No, just stay with Kisses, okay?

426
00:21:34,400 --> 00:21:36,767
Anyway, I'll work on this later,
okay?

427
00:21:36,900 --> 00:21:38,333
[OMINOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

428
00:21:38,467 --> 00:21:40,200
I'll just go see grandmother.

429
00:21:40,333 --> 00:21:41,933
- Andrew!
- Yes?

430
00:21:42,100 --> 00:21:43,967
Is it true mommy is awake?

431
00:21:44,233 --> 00:21:45,567
Yes.

432
00:21:45,700 --> 00:21:46,900
That's what they said.

433
00:21:47,033 --> 00:21:48,567
- I'm going now.
- I'll just change my clothes.

434
00:21:48,700 --> 00:21:50,100
I'll go, come.

435
00:21:52,167 --> 00:21:53,867
Don't worry, Uncle.

436
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:55,933
I'm not actually worried...

437
00:21:56,067 --> 00:21:59,467
because we'll finally know
what really happened to mommy.

438
00:21:59,600 --> 00:22:02,800
[STIRRING MUSIC CONTINUES]

439
00:22:03,600 --> 00:22:05,867
- Mom...
- Mom...

440
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:09,967
[LIFE MONITOR BEEPING]

441
00:22:10,100 --> 00:22:11,300
Mom...

442
00:22:11,433 --> 00:22:13,200
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

443
00:22:13,333 --> 00:22:14,967
Mom, we're here.

444
00:22:18,667 --> 00:22:20,300
Doc, why is she like this?

445
00:22:20,433 --> 00:22:22,400
I thought mommy was okay?

446
00:22:22,533 --> 00:22:25,767
People coming out of coma
are usually like that,

447
00:22:25,900 --> 00:22:27,567
awake but not yet able to talk.

448
00:22:27,700 --> 00:22:29,867
Is there anything we could do,
Doc?

449
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:32,067
For now, nothing.

450
00:22:32,200 --> 00:22:34,467
But to be honest,
this is a good sign

451
00:22:34,600 --> 00:22:37,400
that she's on the road
to recovery.

452
00:22:37,533 --> 00:22:40,400
But to be sure,
we need to run some tests.

453
00:22:40,533 --> 00:22:42,200
Who can go to
the nurse's station

454
00:22:42,333 --> 00:22:43,567
to sign some documents?

455
00:22:43,700 --> 00:22:44,967
I will, Doc.

456
00:22:45,200 --> 00:22:47,967
I'll also talk to Tomas
about what happened.

457
00:22:48,100 --> 00:22:52,067
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

458
00:23:00,900 --> 00:23:02,267
Mom...

459
00:23:04,100 --> 00:23:05,667
Mom, can you hear me?

460
00:23:09,567 --> 00:23:11,833
Please squeeze my hand
if you do, Mom.

461
00:23:13,733 --> 00:23:16,000
Mom, can you wake up now,
please?

462
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:20,267
I promise I'll be good.

463
00:23:21,967 --> 00:23:23,400
Please.

464
00:23:25,033 --> 00:23:27,233
Mom, just come back, please.

465
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:35,833
Mom, I really want to know
who did this to you.

466
00:23:35,967 --> 00:23:39,600
[LIFE MONITOR BEEPING]

467
00:23:45,133 --> 00:23:49,067
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

468
00:24:00,900 --> 00:24:04,533
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

469
00:24:08,500 --> 00:24:11,067
Major Miguel Delgado was
a skilled and honest policeman.

470
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:13,333
He was the type of policeman
who will do everything

471
00:24:13,467 --> 00:24:14,300
for service.

472
00:24:14,433 --> 00:24:16,367
We want to thank everyone.

473
00:24:16,500 --> 00:24:17,500
Send the evidence.

474
00:24:17,633 --> 00:24:19,633
That's Eun Ji,
the owner of this gym.

475
00:24:19,767 --> 00:24:21,200
Hopefully he answers us.

476
00:24:21,333 --> 00:24:22,967
- Eman!
- Eman!

477
00:24:23,100 --> 00:24:24,033
Can we take a picture?

478
00:24:24,167 --> 00:24:26,100
Let's go, we're looking
for Jin Ho.
